# ============================================================================
# synOUT Environment Configuration Template
# NEVER commit plaintext API keys or credentials to this repository.
# Store production values in GitHub Environments (Settings -> Environments -> production)
# or in your runtime deployment secret manager.
#
# NOTE ON USER EMAIL DISPATCH:
# Firebase credentials are NOT required. End users connect their own Gmail,
# Outlook, Yahoo, iCloud, Proton, or custom email directly in the UI during
# their session so synOUT sends opt-out notices on their behalf.
# ============================================================================

# Optional Server-Side AI Key (For synOUT custom statutory notice refinement)
GEMINI_API_KEY=""

# Public Application Base URL
APP_URL=""

# Optional Public Google OAuth 2.0 Web Client ID (Leave commented out — NOT required!)
# End users can send via 1-Click Webmail or 2-Step App Code right out of the box with zero setup.
# VITE_GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=""

# Optional Advanced Self-Hosting Overrides (Leave commented out — NOT required!)
# synOUT automatically finds and launches its built-in headless Chromium browser out of the box
# to fill out broker forms and check required boxes on your behalf with zero setup.
# Only uncomment these if deploying to a custom Linux/Docker server with non-standard paths:
# PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH=""
# BROWSER_WORKER_URL=""
# SYNOUT_DISABLE_BROWSER_WORKER=""

# Optional Server-Side Contact Form Email Provider (For standalone public Contact page delivery to synovamedia@gmail.com)
# Leave commented out unless configuring dedicated server-side contact email transport in deployment secrets:
# CONTACT_SMTP_HOST=""
# CONTACT_SMTP_PORT="465"
# CONTACT_SMTP_USER=""
# CONTACT_SMTP_PASS=""
# CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=""
# CONTACT_RESEND_API_KEY=""
# CONTACT_SENDGRID_API_KEY=""


